   2301  f754							; ==============================================================================
   2302  f754							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   2303  f754							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   2304  f754							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   2305  f754							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   2306  f754							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   2307  f754							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   2308  f754							;
   2309  f754							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   2310  f754							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   2311  f754							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   2312  f754							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   2313  f754							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   2314  f754							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   2315  f754							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   2316  f754							;
   2317  f754							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   2318  f754							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   2319  f754							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   2320  f754							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   2321  f754							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
